\title{darts: Statistical Tools to Analyze Your Darts Game}
\description{
Are you aiming at the right spot in darts? Maybe not! This package estimates the accuracy of your throws from the scores of darts aimed at the center of the board, using EM algorithms under a Gaussian model, and then computes a personalized heatmap of expected scores to find your optimal aiming location. Based on Tibshirani, Price, and Taylor (2011) \doi{10.1111/j.1467-985X.2010.00651.x}.
}
\details{
A typical analysis has two steps:
\enumerate{
\item Throw a set of darts aimed at the center of the board, record the
scores, and estimate the spread of your throws with \code{\link[=simpleEM]{simpleEM()}}
(a single variance) or \code{\link[=generalEM]{generalEM()}} (a full covariance matrix).
\item Compute the expected score for every aiming location with
\code{\link[=simpleExpScores]{simpleExpScores()}} or \code{\link[=generalExpScores]{generalExpScores()}}, plot it with
\code{\link[=drawHeatmap]{drawHeatmap()}}, and find the best spot with \code{\link[=aimSpot]{aimSpot()}}.
}
}
